t is the correct handling for this task?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_QA:1790937462.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_0d9ef512697df0da04af0c03\", \"thread_id\": \"1790937414.000152\", \"author_id\": \"U013\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T10:37:42.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U019\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"A loanword is different from an unrequested language change across a whole sentence.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:8508b653\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multilingual-eval-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Multilingual Evaluation — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Language adherence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multilingual-eval-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Language adherence\\n\\n### Q: Does a single English word in a Korean or Japanese answer count as code-switching?\\nNot automatically. Ordinary loanwords are acceptable. Assess the word in context and against the required output language; an unrequested full paragraph in another language is a different issue.\\n\\n### Q: The user code-switched. Should the response mirror it?\\nCheck the explicit output-language requirement and context. User code-switching alone does not settle the score.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:0d37b1fa\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2\", \"title\": \"Multilingual Evaluation — Instructions (v1.2)\", \"sections\": [\"Language adherence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multilingual-eval-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-10T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-10T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Language adherence\\nFor a monolingual requirement, an unexplained paragraph in another language counts against adherence. Check the requested output language and context first. Ordinary loanwords are not automatically code-switching errors; a user mixing languages does not itself define the required output language.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_MULTI_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790861853.000153:923cb61d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in multilingual-eval-announcements at 2026-10-01T13:37:33